From: redC0rvus <111829302+redC0rvus@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 00:10:27 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 04/24] [general] d3d12: 8bpp resolve of k_8 + copy_dest_swap
 reads alpha (A8)

D3D maps A8 to k_8 with LOW_BLUE, which routes alpha to the stored
component; we were reading blue. DOAX2 renders the volleyball court
shadow map into alpha and resolves it as A8, so the court sand was
multiplied by zero and rendered black.

Ported from xenia-canary 2b3f0cb456 onto the 04d5c40d0d resolve.xesli
(byte-identical to the previous bytecode) and recompiled with fxc.
D3D12 only; SPIR-V not regenerated.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
